# Releases

Human-facing versioning policy lives in [DEVELOPER.md](../../DEVELOPER.md) § Releases. This rule is the operational procedure for agents.

## Do not

- Publish to npm unless the human explicitly asked in this session.
- Run `npm publish` outside `scripts/release-npm.ts` unless the human directs otherwise.
- Skip hooks (`--no-verify`) or weaken `prepublishOnly` (clean, build, test per package).
- Invent the active package list from README — use `ACTIVE_PACKAGES` in `scripts/release-npm.ts`.

## Active vs deps-only packages

**Active** (`ACTIVE_PACKAGES` in `scripts/release-npm.ts`): version bump + publish in dependency order (`PUBLISH_ORDER`: `rlp` → … → `vm`).

**Deps-only** (`DEPS_ONLY_PACKAGES`): `client`, `devp2p`, `ethash`, `wallet`, `testdata` — only `@ethereumjs/*` dependency references updated on bump; own version unchanged; not published.

All active packages share the **same new version number** on each release round.

## Command surface

```sh
tsx scripts/release-npm.ts [--bump-version=<version>] [--publish=<tag>] [--scope=<scope>] [--otp=<code>]
```

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| (none) | Publish current versions to npm (`latest`) — typical after manual bump + CHANGELOG prep |
| `--bump-version=<version>` | Bump active package versions and deps; skip publish unless `--publish` is also set |
| `--publish=<tag>` | Publish (default tag: `latest`) |
| `--scope=<scope>` | Fork scope (default `ethereumjs`); see below |
| `--otp=<code>` | npm 2FA one-time password |

**Examples:**

```sh
tsx scripts/release-npm.ts                                    # publish current versions
tsx scripts/release-npm.ts --bump-version=10.1.0              # bump only
tsx scripts/release-npm.ts --bump-version=10.1.0 --publish=latest
tsx scripts/release-npm.ts --bump-version=10.1.1-nightly.1 --publish=nightly
tsx scripts/release-npm.ts --otp=123456
```

## npm authentication

- Script runs `npm whoami` before publish; exits if not authenticated.
- **Interactive:** `npm login` with a granular access token for `@ethereumjs` publish scope.
- **2FA:** pass `--otp=<code>` when required.
- Never commit tokens or `_authToken` entries to the repo.

## Fork releases (`--scope` ≠ `ethereumjs`)

Used by [Feel Your Protocol](https://feelyourprotocol.org) and similar fork scopes. When scope is not `ethereumjs`:

- Rewrites package names: `@ethereumjs/evm` → `@<scope>/evm`
- Rewrites inter-package `dependencies` / `devDependencies` to the new scope
- Rewrites `@ethereumjs/` import paths under each package `src/`
- Skips deps-only packages (not published; rewriting would break local dev)
- Publishes with `--access=public`

The `--scope` flag is generic; not tied to a specific npm org.

## CHANGELOG updates

Update **every** active package `CHANGELOG.md` for the release, even when a package had no user-facing changes.

### Version header

Add a new section at the top for the target version and release date (date = day of release, agreed with the human).

### One bullet per squash-merged PR

Since `master` uses squash merges, **one commit since the last release tag ≈ one PR**. One bullet per included PR.

**Format:**

```markdown
- Short user-facing summary, see PR [#NNNN](https://github.com/ethereumjs/ethereumjs-monorepo/pull/NNNN)
```

### Include in bullets

- User-facing behavior, API, or default changes
- New or dropped Node.js or TypeScript version support
- External dependency version bumps (npm packages **outside** the monorepo)

### Omit from bullets (skip the PR entirely)

- Documentation-only changes
- Changes confined to `examples/`
- Tests-only changes
- Lint, spellcheck, CI, or other tooling/infrastructure-only PRs

### Packages with no included PRs

Still add a CHANGELOG section for that package:

```markdown
- Maintenance release, no active changes
```

### Finding commits since last release

Use the last release date and/or commit hash the human provides, or compare against the previous release tag in [tags](https://github.com/ethereumjs/ethereumjs-monorepo/tags).

## Typical maintainer flow

1. Human decides version and release date.
2. Agent (or maintainer) updates CHANGELOGs per rules above.
3. `--bump-version` updates `package.json` files and internal `@ethereumjs/*` refs.
4. Human reviews; then publish with `tsx scripts/release-npm.ts` (or bump + publish in one step).
